{"content":[{"c":["FORTUNATUS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Member of the church at Corinth. Fortunatus is a Roman proper name written in Greek and found only once in the NT (",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.16.17","r":"1Cor.16.17","rawR":"1Cor.16.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.16.17","value":"1Cor.16.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 16:17"},"). Paul rejoiced that he, along with Stephanas and Achaicus, had come to be with him in Ephesus. The Textus Receptus has a subscript naming these three men as the carriers of Paul’s letter to the Corinthians."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Fortunatus","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Cor 16:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.16.17","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.16.17","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.16.17"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0656e4ca5dd97295347e734db03eb507b180636b1d1ba1747fec084bfb5676b5","sourceItemName":"Fortunatus","sourceItemOrder":72,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Fortunatus","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Fortunatus","title":"Fortunatus","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}